sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor CU as Customer
    actor CS as CS Agent
    participant UI as Returns Console<br/>(in-house)
    participant EL as Eligibility Engine
    participant RS as Returns Service
    participant BA as Bosta Adapter
    participant WH as Warehouse QC
    participant FE as Financial Engine
    participant LD as Vendor Ledger
    participant SP as Shopify

    Note over CU,SP: Requirement 5 - IN-HOUSE, replacing E-stebdal.<br/>Scenario 3: Return Request -> Confirm Return (CS) -> Ready-To-Pick -> Under Return (3PL) -> Returned (WH)

    alt Phase 1 - CS-operated (how they work today)
        CU->>CS: calls / WhatsApps requesting return
        CS->>UI: create return request on customer's behalf
    else Phase 1b - customer self-service
        CU->>UI: order number + phone lookup (no account)
    end

    UI->>EL: check eligibility(order_item)
    EL->>EL: return window elapsed?
    EL->>EL: vendor policy allows this category?
    EL->>EL: item already returned / exchanged?

    alt ineligible
        EL-->>UI: reject with specific reason
        UI-->>CU: explain why + policy text
        Note right of UI: Rejections are logged.<br/>"Refused - Policy Not Available"<br/>appears 119x in the sheet -<br/>this is where that goes away.
    end

    EL-->>UI: eligible
    CS->>UI: select reason from 56-value taxonomy
    Note right of UI: Reasons carry stakeholder attribution<br/>(Commercial / Marketing / Customer<br/>Behavior / Ops / CS / 3PL) - ported<br/>verbatim from the sheet.

    UI->>RS: createReturnRequest(type = return)
    RS->>RS: INSERT RETURN_REQUESTS + RETURN_ITEMS
    RS->>RS: order_item status -> Return Requested

    CS->>UI: Confirm Return
    RS->>RS: status -> Ready-To-Pick
    RS->>BA: create REVERSE pickup AWB
    Note right of BA: Same shipment adapter as forward<br/>shipping - one integration, both<br/>directions.
    BA-->>RS: reverse tracking number
    RS->>RS: status -> Under Return

    BA->>RS: webhook - picked up / in transit
    BA->>RS: webhook - delivered to warehouse

    RS->>WH: raise QC receipt task
    WH->>UI: inspect item

    alt QC accepted
        WH->>RS: qc_outcome = accepted
        RS->>RS: status -> Returned (WH)
        RS->>FE: value the return
        FE->>LD: post RETURN_REVERSAL (reverses SALE)
        Note right of LD: The ORIGINAL financial snapshot is<br/>never mutated. The reversal is a new,<br/>separately dated ledger entry -<br/>so Req 6.3 and 8.7 stay consistent.
        FE->>FE: create REFUND (status = pending)
        Note right of FE: COD refunds in Egypt are manual.<br/>A refund is a LEDGER OBLIGATION<br/>with a settlement step, not an<br/>automatic payment.
        RS->>SP: write return + refund into Shopify
    else QC rejected (damaged / not as described)
        WH->>RS: qc_outcome = rejected
        RS->>LD: no reversal - vendor keeps payment
        RS->>UI: escalate to CS for customer dispute
    end

    opt reason is vendor-attributable
        RS->>LD: post PENALTY entry against vendor
        Note right of LD: e.g. "Defected Item - Vendor Fault"<br/>(115 occurrences). Currently tracked<br/>on a separate sheet by hand.
    end

    RS->>UI: return closed, visible in vendor scorecard
